      *>----------------------------------------------------------------*
      *>    DEFAULT LINKAGE TO BE USED WHEN CALL FROM WEB               *
      *>    LENGTH....: 200                                             * 
      *>    >>> THIS IS A COPY FROM PGMLINK.LK (USED BY OTHER PROGRAMS) *
      *>    >>> IF CHANGE SOMETHING HERE, MUST BE CHANGED INPGMLINK.LK  *
      *>    >>> IF CHANGE SOMETHING HERE, MUST BE CHANGED INPGMLINK.WS  *
      *> ---------------------------------------------------------------*
      *> LK-FLAG-WEB.....: TO IDENTIFY IF THE EXECUTION IS BY WEB/PROMPT*
      *>    S - WEB EXECUTION                                           *
      *>    N - PROMPT EXECUTION                                        *
      *>                                                                *
      *> LK-CALL-WEB.....: TO IDENTIFY IF THE PROGRAM IS CALLED BY      *
      *>                   ANOTHER PROGRAM RUNNING IN WEB MODE          *
      *>    S - YES, IT'S CALLED BY A PROGRAM RUNNING IN WEB MODE       *
      *>    N - NO, IT'S CALLED BY A PROGRAM RUNNING IN PROMPT MODE     *
      *>                                                                *
      *> LK-TTY..........: WHEN WEB MODE, GET THE TTY FROM THE BROWSER  *
      *> LK-PID..........: GET THE LINUX PROCESS IN EXECUTION (PID)     *
      *> LK-GROUP........: THE NAME TO REFER THE COMPANY IN GENERAL     *
      *> LK-GRUPO-REF....: THE MAIN GROUP/HOLDER NAME (IF EXIST)        *
      *> LK-COMPANY......: THE COMPANY'S CODE IN THE SYSTEM             *
      *> LK-BRANCH.......: THE BRANCH OFFICE'S CODE IN THE SYSTEM       *
      *> LK-USERNAME.....: THE LOGIN USED THE GET IN THE SYSTEM         *
      *> LK-CALL-PROGRAM.: THE NAME OF THE PROGRAM CALLED               *
      *> LK-CALL-DATE....: THE DATE OF THE CALL                         *
      *> LK-CALL-TIME....: THE TIME OF THE CALL                         *
      *> LK-MENU-APP.....: THE ABREVIATION OF THE MODULE (SGN,SFI, SAG) *
      *> LK-MENU-GROUP...: THE CODE OF THE MENU (1,2,3,4)               *
      *> LK-MENU-OPTION..: THE MENU OPTION (REFER TO THE PROGRAM)       *
      *> LK-INT-ACCESS...: IDENTIFY IF THE ACCESS LAN OR WAN            *
      *>----------------------------------------------------------------* 

       01  WL-WEB-PARAMETERS.	
           05  WL-FLAG-WEB              PIC  X(001).
           05  WL-CALL-WEB              PIC  X(001).
           05  WL-TTY                   PIC  X(010).
           05  WL-PID                   PIC  9(005).
           05  WL-GROUP                 PIC  X(010).
           05  WL-GROUP-REF             PIC  X(010).
           05  WL-COMPANY               PIC  9(003).
           05  WL-BRANCH                PIC  9(003).
           05  WL-USERNAME              PIC  X(010).
           05  WL-CALL-PROGRAM          PIC  X(006).
           05  WL-CALL-DATE             PIC  9(008).
           05  WL-CALL-TIME             PIC  9(008).
           05  WL-MENU-APP              PIC  X(003).
           05  WL-MENU-GROUP            PIC  9(002).
           05  WL-MENU-OPTION           PIC  9(002). 
           05  WL-INT-ACCESS            PIC  X(001).
           05  WL-FUNCTION              PIC  X(020).
           05  WL-FUNCTION-BACK         PIC  X(020).
           05  WL-FLAG-FUNCTION         PIC  X(001). 
           05  WL-FILLER                PIC  X(076).
            